      Exterior Door Sill Pan Flashing &amp; Water Infiltration Prevention
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      More than 80% of structural subfloor, rim joist, and foundation plate rot in residential construction originates beneath exterior doorways. When wind-driven rain beats against patio or entry doors, water forces its way past exterior caulking and threshold seals. A <strong>sloped sill pan flashing system with an integrated interior back-dam</strong> is your home's last line of defense—safely catching and ejecting intruding water before it destroys structural framing.
    </p>

    <!-- Key Metrics Grid -->
